## 6. RESTRICTIONS & COMPATIBILITY:
restrictions:
  max_io_current: "500mA"
  total_current_limit: "500mA"
  warnings[9]:
    - "NX1P2-9024DT1 uses control engine '9' which provides ONLY single-axis PTP (Point-to-Point) motion — it does NOT support synchronized motion control (electronic gearing, electronic cam, linear interpolation, circular interpolation, or multi-axis coordinated control); those features require the NX1P2-1040DT1 (2 sync axes) or NX1P2-1140DT1 (4 sync axes); substituting control engine 9 in an application requiring synchronized motion will cause MC_GearIn, MC_CamIn, and MC_MoveLinear instructions to fail with unsupported instruction errors"
    - "The 10 built-in transistor outputs (Q00-Q09) are PNP sourcing (DT1 suffix) and CANNOT generate high-speed pulse output — the built-in transistor response time is 0.5ms ON / 1.0ms OFF which limits output frequency to approximately 500Hz; for stepper or servo pulse train output (up to 500 kpps or 4 Mpps) install a NX-PG0112 (NPN, 500kpps) or NX-PG0232-5 (line driver, 4Mpps) NX unit on the NX bus expansion; attempting to use built-in DO for PTO will produce incorrect pulse counts at any industrial stepping frequency"
    - "The NX1P2-9024DT1 has NO built-in High-Speed Counter (HSC) on the integrated I/O — the built-in 14 digital inputs have a maximum response speed of 20µs and cannot capture encoder signals; for quadrature encoder feedback (A/B), install NX-EC0112 (NPN) or NX-EC0122 (PNP) incremental encoder input units on the NX bus or connect encoder drives directly as EtherCAT slaves; using built-in inputs for encoder pulse counting will cause missed counts at any motor speed above approximately 25Hz"
    - "The NX bus power supply capacity is a MAXIMUM of 10W at 80% efficiency — the CPU provides this power to NX units on the right-side CPU rack; most NX digital I/O units ALSO require a separate I/O power supply; many NX-ID (DI), NX-OD (DO), NX-AD (AI), NX-DA (AO) screwless terminal units require an NX-PF0630 or NX-PF0730 Additional I/O Power Supply Unit; failure to install required NX-PF units causes I/O power faults and all affected NX units will not operate; always consult the NX-PF requirement table in the official datasheet before configuring the NX unit lineup"
    - "The NX1P2-9024DT1 has NO isolation between the 24VDC supply terminal and the internal CPU circuit — the CPU power supply, NX bus power, and built-in I/O power all share the same 24VDC reference; this means ground faults from the external 24VDC supply will propagate directly into the CPU and I/O circuits; always use a SELV-rated industrial 24VDC power supply with proper earth bonding; do NOT share the 24VDC supply rail with power circuits driving motors or solenoids without appropriate filtering"
    - "The RTC (Real-Time Clock) requires the CJ1W-BAT01 battery which is sold separately and NOT included with the controller — without the battery installed, the RTC resets to its default time on every power cycle; any program logic using clock data (scheduling, time-stamped logs, event timestamps) will produce incorrect timestamps; additionally Retain-attribute variables are NOT guaranteed to be preserved across power cycles without battery; replace the battery while power is ON to avoid RTC reset during replacement"
    - "The EtherCAT master port on the NX1P2-9024DT1 supports a maximum of 16 EtherCAT slave nodes — each servo drive, EtherCAT coupler (NX-ECC), GX remote I/O station, and safety FSoE device counts as one EtherCAT slave; a single NX-ECC coupler with 8 NX units behind it counts as 1 slave node (not 9); if more than 16 EtherCAT slaves are required, upgrade to the NJ5 series which supports 64 or more EtherCAT slaves; exceeding 16 nodes causes EtherCAT initialization to fail and all affected drives will go to SAFE-OP state"
    - "The option board slot on the NX1P2-9024DT1 accepts only ONE option board (the NX1P2-1140DT1 with 40 built-in I/O has 2 slots) — if both serial communication AND analog I/O expansion are needed simultaneously, only one can be installed on the board slot; the second function must be provided via NX bus units (NX-CIF101/105 for serial, NX-AD/NX-DA for analog); plan the option board slot assignment carefully during system design; installing an option board requires power off"
    - "The EtherCAT network REQUIRES double-shielded STP cables (Cat5e or higher with braiding AND aluminum foil) — standard Cat5e UTP cables that are acceptable for EtherNet/IP will cause EtherCAT synchronization errors, DC jitter, and intermittent slave disconnections in electrically noisy environments; Omron specifies AWG26 4-pair LSZH double-shielded cables (e.g. XS6W-6LSZH8SS series) or AWG22 2-pair (XS5W-T421 series); cable shields must be connected at both ends to panel earth; maximum segment length is 100m per hop"
compatibility:
  sw: "Sysmac Studio V1.00+ (primary; all NX1P2 features); Sysmac Studio Safety extension (FSoE/safety CPU); CX-One (legacy, read-only for variable mapping only); GX Works3 NOT applicable (Omron, not Mitsubishi)"
  languages: "Ladder Diagram (LD);Structured Text (ST);Function Block Diagram (FBD);Sequential Function Chart (SFC);Instruction List (IL)"
  frameworks: "IEC61131-3;PLCopen-Motion-Control-single-axis;EtherCAT-FSoE;EtherNet-IP-CIP;FINS;Modbus-TCP;IO-Link-via-NX-ILM;CC-Link-via-GX-adapter;Sysmac;IEC61508;ISO13849-PLd"
  certifications: "CE-EN61131-2;cULus-UL61010-2-201-ANSI-ISA12.12.01;RCM;KC;EAC;NK-LR-shipbuilding;RoHS"

